Package: xtpqroot
Type: Package
Title: Panel Quantile Unit Root Tests with Common Shocks and Structural Breaks
Version: 1.0.0
Authors@R: person("Muhammad", "Alkhalaf", email = "muhammedalkhalaf@gmail.com",
    role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"),
    comment = c(ORCID = "0009-0002-2677-9246"))
Description: Implements two panel unit root tests designed for data with
    cross-sectional dependence. The CIPS(tau) test extends Pesaran's (2007)
    CIPS test to a quantile regression framework, allowing analysis of
    asymmetric persistence across different quantiles of the conditional
    distribution, following Yang, Wei and Cai (2022)
    <doi:10.1016/j.econlet.2022.110809> and Nazlioglu et al. (2026). The tFR
    test combines the fractional Fourier function with the logistic smooth
    transition (LST) function to capture both smooth and sharp structural
    breaks simultaneously, following Corakci and Omay (2023)
    <doi:10.1016/j.renene.2023.01.119>. The panel must be strongly balanced.
